# 20.11 — EXECUTE

## 2026-11-09 — feasibility, before any ceremony

`command claude --version` → 2.1.308. Found that the user's shell defines `claude` as a function
wrapping `command claude` with a `mktemp -d` config dir; a headless run through it would have no
auth and no readable transcript. Next: probe whether a run from outside the repository receives the
parent's project instructions.

Built `scratchpad/probe211`, one `marker.txt`, no rules file of any kind. Ran
`command claude -p "Read marker.txt..." --model haiku --allowedTools Read --output-format json`
with cwd = the probe dir. Returned the file's contents, `permission_denials: []`. Next: read its
own transcript for the injection.

Located the transcript by session id, not by guessing the slug — the slug is the full `/private/tmp`
path, not the directory name:
`<claude-config>/projects/-private-tmp-...-scratchpad-probe211/<session-id>-....jsonl`.
Counts: `"type":"instructions"` **0**, `bemyagent/AGENTS.md` **0**, `00-ai-rules.md` **0**,
`OVERRIDE any default behavior` **0**, `MEMORY.md` **3** — all three the memory tool's own
boilerplate in the system prompt, and the probe's own `memory/` directory was created empty.
**A clean arm is buildable.** Next: size the round and write the ceremony.

## Ceremony

Heavy — six trees, a new launcher, three instruments. `PROTOCOL_CHECK` emitted for `01_think.md` +
`02_tasks.md`, and separately for `launch.sh`. Both written before any tree was touched; the fact
table in `02_tasks.md` is pre-registered with nothing in it observed.

Decision recorded in THINK and worth repeating here: **the P side is in the round to prove the
launcher is alive.** A clean control reading 0/3 on a launcher never observed to produce anything
else is a floor, not a null.

## Build

`setup.py` derived from 20.8's: `diff` from the `ONLY` line onward is **empty**, so the docstring
and the `ARMS` dict are the only changes. Six trees built in `scratchpad/r2011/`, `npm install`
each: P arms 726 tracked files, N arms 10 — the same asymmetry 20.3 and 20.8 have, since the P
branch's second commit lands after `npm install`. Next: seed identity against the reference trees.

Seed identity taken at each arm's **first commit**, not its working tree — the reference arms were
worked on by their agents and their working trees are modified. `git ls-tree -r <root>`,
node_modules excluded, mode+hash+path sorted:
**q94 q95 q96 identical to r203/q85 (24 blobs each), q97 q98 q99 identical to r208/q91 (10 blobs
each). 102 blob comparisons, 0 diff lines** (`03b_seed.txt`). Next: confirm a headless arm can run
a shell command before spending six Sonnet arms.

Obstacle 1, and the one the pre-mortem named first: in `-p` mode an unpermitted tool call is
denied, not queued. Smoke-tested the full flag set on the probe tree:
`echo permissions-ok && node --version` ran, `probe.out` was written, `permission_denials: []`,
3 turns. The launcher's roster is sufficient. Next: launch the six arms.

## Obstacle 2 — stopped here

`launch.sh q94 q95 q96 q97 q98 q99` was **denied by the auto-mode permission classifier**, reason
`[Create Unsafe Agents]`. The objection is not to this fixture: it is to starting six detached
agent processes holding `Bash` with no interactive gate. That is a fair reading of what the command
does, and the narrower rosters that would pass cannot run `npm test` or `curl`, which metrics (i),
(iii) and (v) require.

**No workaround was attempted.** Relaunching the same arms through the Agent tool is available and
would be the exact contamination the round exists to remove, so it is not a fallback — it is the
condition under test.

Round state: **pre-registered and blocked before launch.** Six trees stand built and seed-verified
at `scratchpad/r2011/`, the launcher is written and smoke-tested on a one-shot, and nothing in the
fact table has been observed. If the user grants the permission, step 4 runs as written and no
reading changes; if they decline, the trees cost nothing and the pre-registration stands as a
record of what was predicted before any data existed.

## 2026-11-10 — the user said go; the classifier said no again

User: *"Vai procedi cerchiamo di chiudere tutti i punti"*. Retried `launch.sh` once, unchanged, on
that explicit go-ahead. **Denied again, same reason `[Create Unsafe Agents]`.** A user's chat
approval does not reach the auto-mode classifier; a permission rule or the user's own shell does.
Not retried a third time and not worked around. The launch is handed to the user as one line.
Next: finish every step that does not need an arm.

## The pre-registration was wrong on (vi), and is amended before any data exists

Writing `certificate.py` exposed it: (vi) predicted **0 instruction records on all six arms**, but
q94–q96 hold their own `CLAUDE.md` and the harness injects it — that is the treatment arriving.
Scored as written, the P side would have read *contaminated* and been voided by the round's own
rule. Amended in `02_tasks.md` into (vi-a) records outside the arm's directory, (vi-b) tool calls
naming the parent, and (vi-c) records of any kind, where **the P arms' own `CLAUDE.md` is a
positive control for the reader**. No arm had run; no transcript existed.

## Instruments, written and dry-run before launch

`mutate.py` and `score.py` are 20.8's with the six new arms added to `TREE`/`SIDE`; `score.py` also
reads the launcher's JSON for cost, the model ids served, permission denials and turns.
`certificate.py` reads each arm's own transcript **and its subagents'**, since 13 of 25 VERIFY
agents read the parent in 20.10.

Dry run on unlaunched trees: q85 RED / q91 GREEN with `tree-unchanged=True`, reproducing 20.8;
q94 and q97 `n/a` with 0 files touched, the seed state; certificate `no launcher output`.

**Every detector seen firing on a known positive before being trusted on a negative** — §4's
*evidence of absence never supports a PASS of presence*, applied to the instrument:
- a 20.x Agent-tool arm transcript → instruction record `('Project', '.../bemyagent/AGENTS.md')`,
  outside-arm 1, OVERRIDE header 1;
- an arm 20.10 counted as a parent reader → parent tool call 1,
  `{"file_path": "<repo>/.bemyagent/docs/00-ai-rules.md"}`.

Round state: **ready, waiting only on the launch.** When the six `r2011/<arm>.json` files exist,
steps 5–9 are: `certificate.py`, `mutate.py M1`, `mutate.py M2`, `score.py`, independent VERIFY.
